WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:04.457
Ally was still talking to Barry and Mateo about the cook-off.

2
00:00:04.458 --> 00:00:10.331
"If we win the contest, I'm going to use my prize money for cooking classes," Barry said.

3
00:00:10.332 --> 00:00:15.514
"And I'm going to buy a collector's edition of the first Cosmic Quest comic book.

4
00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:18.378
They're expensive!" Mateo said.

5
00:00:18.379 --> 00:00:20.959
"What about you, Ally?" Barry asked.

6
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.452
Ally scratched her head. "I can't think of anything I need."

7
00:00:25.453 --> 00:00:28.764
"I bet you'll come up with something," Barry said.

8
00:00:28.765 --> 00:00:33.382
"So, tell us more about Food Truck Rally , Barry," Ally

9
00:00:33.383 --> 00:00:38.903
said. "Yeah, what other local food trucks are going to be in the contest?" Mateo

10
00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:42.525
asked. "They sent me a list." Barry pulled out his

11
00:00:42.526 --> 00:00:48.657
phone. "There's Taco Nation, Gimme the Beef, Ella's Eats, the Food Dude, and

12
00:00:48.658 --> 00:00:52.200
us." "That's only five food trucks," Ally

13
00:00:52.201 --> 00:00:55.782
said. "You said that the contest was among six

14
00:00:55.783 --> 00:00:58.970
trucks." "You're right." Barry scanned the list

15
00:00:58.971 --> 00:01:01.901
again. "Oh," he said, biting his

16
00:01:01.902 --> 00:01:04.083
lip. "I didn't see the last truck on the

17
00:01:04.084 --> 00:01:07.720
list." "So, who is it?" Mateo

18
00:01:07.721 --> 00:01:09.492
asked. Barry held up his

19
00:01:09.493 --> 00:01:14.281
phone. "What?" Mateo's eyes went wide as he stared at the

20
00:01:14.282 --> 00:01:19.378
screen. "Pepe's? Since when do they have a food truck?"

21
00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:23.333
Barry shrugged. "Their website says it's brand-new."

22
00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:28.088
Ally's eyes flashed. "Pepe's almost cost Ray his business once!

23
00:01:28.089 --> 00:01:30.288
We cannot let them win.

24
00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:38.038
Barry, you should come up with something really fantastic to serve at the contest, something guaranteed to win!"

25
00:01:38.039 --> 00:01:43.016
"Yeah," Mateo said. "Something that no one will be expecting."

26
00:01:43.017 --> 00:01:48.757
"I'm already on it!" Barry hurried out of the diner.

27
00:01:48.758 --> 00:01:52.742
"So, let's talk about our double date," Mateo said to Ally.

28
00:01:52.743 --> 00:01:56.454
"What do kids on Astralia do on dates?"

29
00:01:56.455 --> 00:02:00.251
"Stardust catching is really popular," Ally said.

30
00:02:00.252 --> 00:02:05.362
"We wear special spacesuits and collect stardust."

31
00:02:05.363 --> 00:02:08.585
"That sounds like fun," Mateo said.

32
00:02:08.586 --> 00:02:14.701
"But we've got too much gravity here on Earth to go stardust catching."

33
00:02:14.702 --> 00:02:18.364
"Are you going to take my advice and plan a double date?"

34
00:02:18.365 --> 00:02:20.785
Flo asked as she came out of the kitchen.

35
00:02:20.786 --> 00:02:24.468
Ally nodded. "We're trying to think of what to do."

36
00:02:24.469 --> 00:02:28.988
"What about going to the park on Saturday night to watch the lunar eclipse?

37
00:02:28.989 --> 00:02:31.730
You can have a picnic," Flo said.

38
00:02:31.731 --> 00:02:35.371
She looked up as two customers walked into the diner.

39
00:02:35.372 --> 00:02:38.539
"You stay here, Ally. I'll get their order."

40
00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:40.974
"Thanks, Flo," Ally said.

41
00:02:40.975 --> 00:02:46.343
"I'm always here for you, Ally." Flo hurried off.

42
00:02:46.344 --> 00:02:49.353
"I like Flo's idea," Mateo said.

43
00:02:49.354 --> 00:02:51.979
"Ally, you should just call Julius.

44
00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.899
Girls ask boys out on dates all the time here."

45
00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:04.103
"We do too on Astralia, but I don't have time to spend a full day serenading him in public."

46
00:03:04.104 --> 00:03:07.445
"Huh?" Mateo looked confused.

47
00:03:07.446 --> 00:03:11.151
"That's what we do on Astralia," Ally said.

48
00:03:11.152 --> 00:03:17.407
"We follow the person around and sing their favorite songs to them all day long."

49
00:03:17.408 --> 00:03:21.376
"That sounds like a lot," Mateo said.

50
00:03:21.377 --> 00:03:24.812
"Calling him might be easier."

51
00:03:24.813 --> 00:03:27.568
Ally gulped, suddenly worried.

52
00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:30.253
"What if he's changed his mind about me?

53
00:03:30.254 --> 00:03:33.495
Or maybe he figured out that I'm an alien!

54
00:03:33.496 --> 00:03:37.375
Do you think he'd tell Dr. Lloyd?"

55
00:03:37.376 --> 00:03:41.357
"You're being silly," Mateo said.

56
00:03:41.358 --> 00:03:48.317
"Okay, I'll do it." Ally pulled Alpha out of her pocket and powered her up.

57
00:03:48.318 --> 00:03:50.983
"Alpha, call Julius."

58
00:03:50.984 --> 00:03:54.858
Alpha made a snorting sound. "Fine."

59
00:03:54.859 --> 00:03:58.361
Ally held her breath, waiting for Julius to answer.

60
00:03:58.362 --> 00:04:01.771
But after one ring, the line went dead.

61
00:04:01.772 --> 00:04:07.001
"That's strange," Ally said. "Alpha, call Julius."

62
00:04:07.002 --> 00:04:11.574
Again, the phone rang once and went dead.

63
00:04:11.575 --> 00:04:16.390
Ally tried two more times and then gave up. "He

64
00:04:16.391 --> 00:04:19.335
doesn't want to talk to me." Mateo

65
00:04:19.336 --> 00:04:21.097
shook his head. "It's

66
00:04:21.098 --> 00:04:25.457
probably just Alpha glitching again. Try

67
00:04:25.458 --> 00:04:28.192
calling him with my phone." Ally

68
00:04:28.193 --> 00:04:30.528
hesitated. "Do

69
00:04:30.529 --> 00:04:34.262
you want me to call him?" Mateo asked. "No,

70
00:04:34.263 --> 00:04:36.878
that's silly," Ally said. "I'll

71
00:04:36.879 --> 00:04:40.799
do it, but after work and at home, in private. Maybe

72
00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:46.738
I'll be less nervous then." ***

73
00:04:46.739 --> 00:04:50.325
But later, Ally felt just as anxious.

74
00:04:50.326 --> 00:04:54.514
She paced around her room with Mateo's phone in her hand.

75
00:04:54.515 --> 00:04:57.082
"I don't know why I'm so nervous, Alpha.

76
00:04:57.083 --> 00:04:59.009
It's just a phone call.

77
00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:03.039
But what if he picks up this time and I don't know what to say?"

78
00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:07.157
"Preparation is the key to any task," Alpha said.

79
00:05:07.158 --> 00:05:11.974
"You're right, Alpha! I'm glad to see you working perfectly now.

80
00:05:11.975 --> 00:05:14.134
That gives me a good idea.

81
00:05:14.135 --> 00:05:17.671
Write me a script of what to say to Julius."

82
00:05:17.672 --> 00:05:22.385
Alpha growled. "I am not a toy!"

83
00:05:22.386 --> 00:05:24.765
"I know," Ally said.

84
00:05:24.766 --> 00:05:28.617
"But your prime directive is to assist me."

85
00:05:28.618 --> 00:05:30.846
"Fine." Alpha grumbled.

86
00:05:30.847 --> 00:05:33.533
A short script appeared on the screen.

87
00:05:33.534 --> 00:05:36.891
"Thank you!" Ally said.

88
00:05:36.892 --> 00:05:44.121
"I'm finally ready to make this call!"

